Subject: [PATCH 15/16] infiniti: document the dropped private-space priv-apps

The OOS private-space cluster ships three system_ext priv-apps
(com.oplus.pantanal.ums, com.oplus.phonemanager, com.oplus.exsystemservice)
that this tree does not ship. They are not load-bearing for the camera port,
and shipping them without privapp-permissions allowlist entries bootloops
system_ready under enforce; dropping them is the safer, de-bloating choice.
Record the decision, the boot-risk rationale, and a TODO for a future
stub-based accommodation so the drop is not mistaken for an oversight.

(cherry picked from commit 2e0030f35f906d6c049c3499a3d0e8fd594f35e9)
